4.7uF/25V, while the other bulk/decoupling caps on the EPD sheet are 1uF/25V and the spec lists C1 at 1 \u00b5F/25 V (default value set).\",\n      \"expected\": \"Per the spec, the boost/charge-pump capacitor values should be 1 \u00b5F/25 V (default set), with the G1-specific 1 \u00b5F/6.3 V part at C2/C17.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"C1 4.7uF/25V on EPD_Driver sheet (page 3)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"| C2 default: 1 \u00b5F/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 \u00b5F/25 V | Matches default |\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"A 4.7 \u00b5F capacitor in the boost/charge-pump node changes the ripple and charge-transfer behaviour of the EPD high-voltage generator relative to the reference design. This is a minor effect, but it is a deviation from the stated value.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The keyboard column COL3 (NET0057) is labelled onto the drain of the display-power P-MOSFET on the same sheet, which shorts the switched EPD power node to the keyboard matrix and contradicts the spec's separate Display_Power_Switch net. A lower-confidence value deviation (C1 at 4.7 \u00b5F rather than 1 \u00b5F) is also noted.\"\n}",
